{"id": "Dey1eScxTRG", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why is Hanuman ji covered in sindoor? 🧡 The legend every dadi knows (and the reason we still offer him the chola).\n\nOne morning in Ayodhya, Hanuman saw Maa Sita putting sindoor in her hair. \"Maa, why the sindoor?\" \"It's for Shri Ram's long life.\"\n\nHanuman thought: if a pinch gives him a long life… what would ALL of me do? So he covered himself in sindoor, head to toe… to tail. And walked into Ram's court like that.\n\nThe whole court laughed. Ram asked, \"Hanuman, what is all this?\" Hanuman joined his hands: \"A pinch gives you a long life. I want you to live forever.\"\n\nRam's eyes filled with tears. He hugged him and blessed him: whoever offers Hanuman sindoor will have Ram's blessing.\n\nThat's why Hanuman ji's murtis are orange: devotees offer the chola, sindoor mixed with chameli oil, on Tuesdays and Saturdays.\n\n(It's a legend told in temples and homes, not a verse from the Valmiki Ramayana or the Ramcharitmanas.)\n\n📚 15K FAMILY DEAL: Rishi Katha Books 1–3 for ₹350 (instead of ₹500), only till 25 Oct, midnight. Comment FAMILY and we'll DM you the deal, or tap the link in bio: rishikatha.com\n\nTuesday or Saturday: when do YOU visit Hanuman ji? Tell us in the comments 👇 Save this for your kids, and share it with someone who says \"Jai Bajrangbali\" 🙏\n\n#hanuman #hanumanji #bajrangbali #jaishreeram #sindoor #hanumanchalisa #ramayana #sitaram #mythology #indianmythology #hindumythology #kidsstories #rishikatha #bedtimestories #tuesday", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792667249, "like_count": 48212, "comment_count": 145, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1109402178556536a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 50.891, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/